{#-
  Typed System.Diagnostics.Activity setter extensions, one class per registry root, and one
  value-set struct per enum attribute. Each setter calls Activity.SetTag with the
  registry-defined key and a strongly-typed value; for `template[...]` attributes the setter
  takes a `segment` parameter to compose the runtime key.

  Registry enums are open value sets, so an enum attribute's type is a readonly struct with one
  static member per value and an explicit `Custom` escape hatch (QYL0121 reports a Custom value
  equal to a member). There is no conversion from a literal: a string has to name a member or go
  through Custom on purpose. The const-string `…Values` classes live under Generated/Attributes
  only, where switch and pattern matching use them.
-#}
